---
import CodeBlock from "@/components/page/CodeBlock.astro";
---

<section class="site-frame py-16 sm:py-24" x-data="portCommands">
  <div class="flex max-w-2xl flex-col gap-3">
    <h2 class="text-pretty text-2xl font-medium -tracking-[0.4px] xl:text-3xl">
      Killing a port from the terminal
    </h2>
    <p class="text-pretty text-foreground-muted">
      Two commands, no app required. Find what's holding the port, then stop it by process id.
      Change the port below and the commands update, so you can copy the ones you actually need
      rather than editing 3000 out of them.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 sm:mt-10">
    <label class="text-[13px] font-medium text-foreground" for="port-input">Port</label>
    <input
      id="port-input"
      type="text"
      inputmode="numeric"
      autocomplete="off"
      spellcheck="false"
      maxlength="5"
      value="3000"
      x-model="port"
      class="w-24 rounded-lg border border-border bg-background-raised px-3 py-1.5 font-mono text-[13px] text-foreground outline-none transition-colors focus-visible:border-border-strong focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:-outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-primary"
    />
    <span class="text-[13px] text-foreground-soft" x-show="!valid" x-cloak>
      Using 3000 until that's a port between 1 and 65535.
    </span>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-6 grid max-w-3xl gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="text-[13px] font-medium text-foreground">1. See what's on the port</span>
      <CodeBlock
        code="lsof -i :3000"
        expression="`lsof -i :${value}`"
        label="Copy the lsof command"
      />
      <p class="text-[13px]/relaxed text-foreground-soft">
        The <code class="rounded bg-foreground/[0.06] px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-[12px]">PID</code>
        column is the process id you want.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="flex flex-col gap-2">
      <span class="text-[13px] font-medium text-foreground">2. Stop it</span>
      <CodeBlock code="kill 10791" label="Copy the kill command" />
      <p class="text-[13px]/relaxed text-foreground-soft">
        Swap in the id from step 1. Add <code
          class="rounded bg-foreground/[0.06] px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-[12px]">-9</code
        > only if it ignores you, since that skips cleanup.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="mt-8 flex max-w-3xl flex-col gap-2 sm:mt-10">
    <span class="text-[13px] font-medium text-foreground">Or both at once</span>
    <CodeBlock
      code="lsof -ti:3000 | xargs kill"
      expression="`lsof -ti:${value} | xargs kill`"
      label="Copy the one-line command"
    />
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-[13px]/relaxed text-foreground-soft">
      Fine when you already know the port is yours. It kills everything listening there without
      telling you what any of it was, which is the part Portman exists to fix.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
